From c5e5a1bbdbf9fbc3d7947d8c08abf636c0a6fa70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Intel MPSS <mpss@intel.invalid>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:57:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] micpm: KNC power management (cpufreq, cpuidle, TMU, PM
 SCIF)

From Intel MPSS 3.8.6, drivers/micpm:
 - mic_cpufreq + the knc cpufreq governor: P-states through the SBOX,
   LAPIC recalibration on frequency change, the TMU (thermal) clamp.
 - mic_cpuidle + the mic menu governor: CC1, package C3, and the
   C-step-only CC6/PC6 with their low-memory resume trampolines
   (corec6.S, pc6_trampoline.S; they need a static identity page
   table, level3_ident_pgt in head_64.S).
 - mic_pm/pm_scif: the PM protocol with the host (PC3 needs the host
   PM server's consent), micpm_proc, the RAS registration.
 - Core support: CPUIDLE_FLAG_IGNORE, the clocksource watchdog paused
   around package C3 (the TSC stops), timekeeping_suspended WARN_ONCE.

Adaptations for 6.18:
 - cpufreq: freq-QoS FREQ_QOS_MAX request instead of CPUFREQ_ADJUST
   for the TMU clamp (5.4), policy->freq_table (4.19; set before the
   6.17 table helpers, which take the table from the policy and
   crashed in cpufreq_frequency_table_cpuinfo), no driver-side
   scaling_available_frequencies attribute (6.17 creates it in the
   core; the duplicate made sysfs creation fail and the policy was
   torn down and re-created 240 times), exit() returns void (6.11),
   cpufreq_freq_transition_begin/end, kobj_attribute, freqs->policy.
 - cpuidle: cpuidle_poll_state_init (states start at 1),
   last_residency_ns, governor select() with stop_tick, the enter
   callbacks no longer enable IRQs themselves (6.6 warns on the leaked
   IRQ state and enables after the callback), no XCR0 restore (dead on
   KNC), fix_processor_context() follows 4.19 (cpu_entry_area TSS,
   fixmap GDT), a page placeholder for the gone trampoline_level4_pgt.
 - PC3 timekeeping: the TSC keeps running through PC3 on B1, so
   clocksource_tsc is CLOCK_SOURCE_SUSPEND_NONSTOP and
   timekeeping_resume() recovers the idle time from the cycle delta;
   read_persistent_clock() returns {0,0} (no CMOS RTC on the card;
   the garbage timespec tripped "Invalid sleep delta value!" on every
   PC3 exit).
 - proc_ops, SYM_* asm macros, cpufreq_policy_data, mic_menu on
   get_avenrun().

